  nodeTextLayers:
  - Final crystal lattice resembles a honeycomb if observed from the z-axis, which
    coincides with the three fold axis of each hexamer.
  - "Mature insulin crystals found in \u03B2 cells are mostly globular, with a diameter
    around 150nm."
  - The insulin crystal displayed here is an interpretation of crystallization deduced
    from in vitro studies; the true structure remains a great technical challenge
    in the field.
